{
  "id": "2KI.18",
  "number": "18",
  "bookId": "2KI",
  "reference": "2 Kings 18",
  "verseCount": 37,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "18",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2KI 18"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "18",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the third year of the reign of Hoshea son of Elah as king of Israel, Hezekiah son of Ahaz became king of Judah ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "at the age of 25, and he ruled in Jerusalem for 29 years. His mother was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Following the example of his ancestor King David, he did what was pleasing to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "NUM.21.9"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Num 21.9",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He destroyed the pagan places of worship, broke the stone pillars, and cut down the images of the goddess Asherah. He also broke in pieces the bronze snake that Moses had made, which was called Nehushtan. Up to that time the people of Israel had burnt incense in its honour. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hezekiah trusted in the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Israel; Judah never had another king like him, either before or after his time. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He was faithful to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and never disobeyed him, but carefully kept all the commands that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had given Moses. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " was with him, and he was successful in everything he did. He rebelled against the emperor of Assyria and refused to submit to him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He defeated the Philistines, and raided their settlements, from the smallest village to the largest city, including Gaza and its surrounding territory.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the fourth year of Hezekiah's reign — which was the seventh year of King Hoshea's reign over Israel — Emperor Shalmaneser of Assyria invaded Israel and besieged Samaria. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the third year of the siege, Samaria fell; this was the sixth year of Hezekiah's reign, and the ninth year of Hoshea's reign. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Assyrian emperor",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18.11",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Assyrian emperor",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": See 17.6.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " took the Israelites to Assyria as prisoners and settled some of them in the city of Halah, some near the River Habor in the district of Gozan, and some in the cities of Media.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Samaria fell because the Israelites did not obey the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " their God, but broke the covenant he had made with them and disobeyed all the laws given by Moses, the servant of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". They would not listen and they would not obey.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the fourteenth year of the reign of King Hezekiah, Sennacherib, the emperor of Assyria, attacked the fortified cities of Judah and conquered them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hezekiah sent a message to Sennacherib, who was in Lachish: “I have done wrong; please stop your attack, and I will pay whatever you demand.” The emperor's answer was that Hezekiah should send him ten tonnes of silver and one tonne of gold. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hezekiah sent him all the silver in the Temple and in the palace treasury; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "he also stripped the gold from the temple doors and the gold with which he himself had covered the doorposts, and he sent it all to Sennacherib. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Assyrian emperor sent a large army from Lachish to attack Hezekiah at Jerusalem; it was commanded by his three highest officials. When they arrived at Jerusalem, they occupied the road where the clothmakers work, by the ditch that brings water from the upper pond. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then they sent for King Hezekiah, and three of his officials went out to meet them: Eliakim son of Hilkiah, who was in charge of the palace; Shebna, the court secretary; and Joah son of Asaph, who was in charge of the records. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the Assyrian officials told them that the emperor wanted to know what made King Hezekiah so confident. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He demanded, “Do you think that words can take the place of military skill and might? Who do you think will help you rebel against Assyria? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You are expecting Egypt to help you, but that would be like using a reed as a walking stick — it would break and jab your hand. That is what the king of Egypt is like when anyone relies on him.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Assyrian official went on, “Or will you tell me that you are relying on the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God? It was the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s shrines and altars that Hezekiah destroyed, when he told the people of Judah and Jerusalem to worship only at the altar in Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will make a bargain with you in the name of the emperor. I will give you 2,000 horses if you can find that many men to ride them! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You are no match for even the lowest ranking Assyrian official, and yet you expect the Egyptians to send you chariots and horsemen! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you think I have attacked your country and destroyed it without the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s help? The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " himself told me to attack it and destroy it.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.25"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Eliakim, Shebna, and Joah told the official, “Speak Aramaic to us, sir. We understand it. Don't speak Hebrew; all the people on the wall are listening.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.26"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He replied, “Do you think you and the king are the only ones the emperor sent me to say all these things to? No, I am also talking to the people who are sitting on the wall, who will have to eat their excrement and drink their urine, just as you will.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the official stood up and shouted in Hebrew, “Listen to what the emperor of Assyria is telling you! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He warns you not to let Hezekiah deceive you. Hezekiah can't save you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And don't let him persuade you to rely on the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". Don't think that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will save you, and that he will stop our Assyrian army from capturing your city. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Don't listen to Hezekiah. The emperor of Assyria commands you to come out of the city and surrender. You will all be allowed to eat grapes from your own vines, and figs from your own trees, and to drink water from your own wells — ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "until the emperor resettles you in a country much like your own, where there are vineyards to give wine and there is corn for making bread; it is a land of olives, olive oil, and honey. If you do what he commands, you will not die, but live. Don't let Hezekiah fool you into thinking that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will rescue you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Did the gods of any other nations save their countries from the emperor of Assyria? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Where are they now, the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivvah? Did anyone save Samaria? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When did any of the gods of all these countries ever save their country from our emperor? Then what makes you think the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " can save Jerusalem?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.35"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The people kept quiet, just as King Hezekiah had told them to; they did not say a word. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 18:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Eliakim, Shebna, and Joah tore their clothes in grief, and went and reported to the king what the Assyrian official had said.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.18.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.18.37"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
